; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Bouncing Ball
; CATEGORY: Science & Simulation
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     physics, gravity, energy, animation, bounce
; SUMMARY:  A ball drops, bounces and loses a little energy with every bounce until it rolls to a stop.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A red ball falls from high up on the left and bounces along the
;   floor, leaving a dotted trail. Every bounce is lower than the one
;   before, because some of the ball's energy turns into sound and heat
;   when it squashes against the floor.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. The height of each hop is printed.
;   Change BOUNCINESS near the bottom (try 0.95 or 0.5) and run again.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * gravity changes speed a little bit every moment
;   * flipping the sign of a number to make something turn around
;   * multiplying by a number less than 1 to make something shrink
;   * WAIT for smooth animation
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the floor a trampoline with BOUNCINESS above 1. What happens?
;   * Change GRAVITY to 0.2 for a Moon ball.
;   * Give the trail a new color after every bounce.
; ============================================================

make "floor -250

to draw.floor
  setpc 8 setpensize 6
  penup setxy -400 :floor - 3 pendown setx 400
  setpensize 1
end

to bounce.ball
  ; x and y are where the ball is, vy is how fast it moves up or down.
  localmake "x -360
  localmake "y 250
  localmake "vy 0
  localmake "bounces 0
  penup setxy :x :y
  showturtle
  ; Keep going until the ball is too tired to bounce, or rolls off.
  while [:x < 390] [
    ; At the very top of a hop the ball is still rising, but gravity is
    ; about to use up the last of that upward speed.
    if and :vy > 0 :vy <= :gravity [
      make "bounces :bounces + 1
      print (sentence [Hop] :bounces [reached] round (:y - :floor - 10) [steps high])
    ]
    ; gravity makes the ball fall faster every tick
    make "vy :vy - :gravity
    make "y :y + :vy
    make "x :x + 1.5
    ; Hit the floor? Put the ball back on top of it and send it up again,
    ; but slower: BOUNCINESS keeps only part of the speed.
    if :y < :floor + 10 [
      make "y :floor + 10
      make "vy (minus :vy) * :bounciness
      ; A real ball stops hopping when the bounces get tiny and just
      ; rolls. Without this line it would keep making hops too small to see.
      if :vy < 2 [make "vy 0]
    ]
    setxy :x :y
    ; leave a dot every few steps so the path stays visible
    if 0 = remainder round :x 6 [dot pos]
    wait 1
  ]
end

make "gravity 0.6
make "bounciness 0.8

clearscreen
setbackground [230 240 255]
draw.floor
setshape "circle
setpc 4
bounce.ball
hideturtle
print [The ball has rolled away.]
